, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and Japan. It offers hard coolers, including the YETI Tundra, YETI Roadie, YETI V Series hard coolers, YETI TANK ice bucket, and YETI Silo 6G water cooler, as well as related accessories comprising locks, dry baskets, beverage holders, and dividers. The company also provides soft cooler bags, such as under the Hopper collection and Daytrip collection; duffel bags, backpacks, luggage, and packing cubes comprising the Panga collection, Crossroads collection, Camino Caryall, SideKick Dry gear case, Cayo collection, and Ranchero collection; cargo and storage solutions that include the LoadOut GoBox, LoadOut bucket, and LoadOut swivel seat names; and outdoor living products, which consist of Trailhead camp chair, Lowlands blanket, Boomer dog bowls, Hondo beach chair, can crusher, and the YETI Fire Pit. In addition, it offers bottles and jugs under the Rambler, Yonder, and Silo collections; cups, mugs, and tumblers under the Rambler collection; Rambler products, including tableware, coffeeware, barware, and containers, as well as insulated bowls and food jars, ceramic-lined mugs and stackable cups, French presses, pitchers, wine chillers, wine tumblers, the beverage bucket, colsters, and cocktail shakers; and cookware. Further, the company provides apparel, such as hats, shirts, and sweatshirts, as well as ice substitutes and other YETI branded products. It sells its products through its direct-to-consumer channel, including websites, corporate sales programs, and retail stores, as well as through its wholesale channel. YETI Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew J. Reintjes | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $153K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["YETI Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.9B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 57% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $212M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 45\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 10.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"YETI Holdings (YETI) Lowers Full Year Outlook After Mixed Third Quarter Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/yeti-holdings-yeti-lowers-full-141320844.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.23,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"What YETI (YETI) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/yeti-yeti-said-q3-earnings-131450489.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575690.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.886,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"YETI (NYSE:YETI) Downgraded by Piper Sandler to Neutral","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/yeti-nyseyeti-downgraded-by-piper-sandler-to-neutral.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572473.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"YETI (YETI) Stock Seems Reasonable On A 63% Five Year Slide","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-yeti/yeti-holdings/news/yeti-yeti-stock-seems-reasonable-on-a-63-five-year-slide","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794558359.349,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.392,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"YETI Q3 2026 deep dive: Cautious outlook as U.S. and Canada d